<title>SOUTH KOREA: BOK offers to sell dlrs in forward trading - dealers.</title>
<headline>BOK offers to sell dlrs in forward trading - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea (BOK) offered to sell dollar in forward trading to slow the won's drop against the U.S. unit, dealers said.</p>
<p>The bank refused to comment.</p>
<p>Dealers said the central bank offered to sell dollars in three-month forward trading at the 876.00 won level and in six-month forward trading at 888.00, they said.</p>
<p>The bank was earlier seen selling dollars on the spot market shortly after the local currency opened trading at 865.00 won.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
